  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CDT Thu Jul 9 2026\n\nA broad upper ridge will build to our west, cutting off a low over\nthe TN valley on Sunday. At the surface, a west/east draped\nboundary will slowly drift south and sustain chances for showers\nand thunderstorms, any of which could produce heavy rain and\nflooding concerns. This cutoff low may linger over the area into\nearly next week and keep higher changes for scattered showers and\nthunderstorms in the forecast. Diurnal activity will then \ncontinue through the week but overall chances for precipitation \nwill be lower as the upper ridge expands over the area.",
